                    <occupation>essayist</occupation>
                    <occupation>translator</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Hayward studied under Godwin's ex-friend <persName key="TWI01">Francis Twiss</persName> in Bath (1807-11) (Twiss 
      had ceased contact after Godwin married Wollstonecraft). Hayward moved to London in 1824. He was called
      to the bar in 1832 and later translated Goethe's <title>Faust</title>, which won him some fame and the friendship of many
      literary luminaries. </p>
